          "path": "_m/r/7/k/c/noosa-national-park-wp/emu-mountain.jpg",
          "filename": "Emu Mountain.jpg",
          "caption": "Emu Moutain is located in the small seaside town of Coolum on the eastern coast of Australia. At 84 metres tall, the mountain is part of the Noosa National Park area which provides a sanctuary for native flora and fauna. Emus no longer live in the region due to urban development and deforestation, however many native Australian reptiles and small mammals thrive in this region due to its proximity to the sea and several small creeks and swamps. This aerial photo, taken with the DJI Phantom 3 Advanced, shows the summit trail of Emu Mountain.",
